  <note>
    <title>Book Review: Deep Work</title>
    <content><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note>
  <div><i>Deep Work by Cal Newport</i></div>
  <div><br/></div>
  <div><b>Core Concept:</b></div>
  <div>The ability to focus without distraction on cognitively demanding tasks is becoming increasingly valuable in our economy at the same time it is becoming increasingly rare.</div>
  <div><br/></div>
  <div><b>Key Takeaways:</b></div>
  <ul>
    <li>Deep work is rare and valuable</li>
    <li>Shallow work is inevitable but should be minimized</li>
    <li>Create rituals and routines for deep work</li>
    <li>Embrace boredom to strengthen focus muscles</li>
  </ul>
  <div><br/></div>
  <div><b>Implementation Ideas:</b></div>
  <ol>
    <li>Schedule deep work blocks: 9am-12pm daily</li>
    <li>Eliminate distractions: turn off notifications</li>
    <li>Create dedicated workspace for focused work</li>
    <li>Practice deliberate practice on core skills</li>
  </ol>
  <div><br/></div>
  <div>Rating: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ (5/5)</div>
</en-note>]]></content>
